  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Web Application - \"Lucky Days\" Fundraiser",
    "description": "View the full write-up on this project at on my portfolio in the link below.\n\nFull-stack design, development and deployment of a web application that processes donations for a non-profit fundraiser called \"Lucky Days\". The end-user is prompted to choose a calendar day out of the year, which they may dedicate to a personal cause, and \"purchase\" it for an entry into a 50/50 raffle. \n\nThis application is the dedicated interface by which the non-profit is collecting donations for their \"Lucky Days\" fundraiser. I worked directly with members of the board to conceptualize a user experience that was simple and intuitive. Once a user selects their \"Lucky Days\", they are directed to a Stripe checkout page which processes the donation. Upon a successful purchase, a raffle ticket is generated and provided to the user for download via email. \n\nAt the end of each calendar month, all the donors who purchased a \"Lucky Day\" are entered into a 50/50 raffle for a chance to win half of the proceedings for that month. In order to keep record of donations and raffle entries, an automated data report is generated which details the month's transactions. \n\nThis application is deployed in a serverless environment and utilizes custom hosting. See the application live and consider making a donation at the link below.",
